      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. it's a good start. one thing though—the client is going to ask for more granular detail. they'll want to know why \"demographic upheaval\" specifically translates to risk in a way that commercial growth doesn't counteract. \n\ncould you expand on the connection between a rising minority population and the \"instability\" you mentioned? specifically, can you tie it to things like tenant turnover, changes in community cohesion, or even the likelihood of decreased maintenance/upkeep in the long run? i need to explain why this demographic shift isn't just a \"change\" but a specific indicator of potential value decline.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
